          </li>
          <li>
            Built tooling to scale Amazon Robotics' simulation infrastructure
            using Docker, RabbitMQ, C, Python, and Java
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="entry">
      <div class="entry-header">
        <div>
          <h3>Tufts JumboCode</h3>
          <p class="org">Medford, MA</p>
        </div>
        <span class="date">Sep 2020 &ndash; Jun 2021</span>
      </div>
      <div class="role">
        <div class="role-header">
          <span>Technical Lead</span>
        </div>
        <ul>
          <li>
            Led a 12-developer team building a medical resource finder web
            application
          </li>
          <li>
            Reviewed 3&ndash;5 pull requests weekly and mentored developers on
            technical decisions
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="entry">
      <div class="entry-header">
        <div>
          <h3>Codio</h3>
          <p class="org">Cambridge, MA</p>
        </div>
        <span class="date">Jun 2020 &ndash; Aug 2020</span>
      </div>
      <div class="role">
        <div class="role-header">
          <span>Content and Code Development Intern</span>
        </div>
        <ul>
          <li>
            Developed auto-grading API for Processing programs using an abstract
